{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q4634186","formula":"C₁₁H₉N₃O","hill":"C11H9N3O","elements":["H","C","N","O"],"composition":{"C":11.0,"H":9.0,"N":3.0,"O":1.0},"names":{"en":"3-Pyridylnicotinamide"},"descriptions":{"en":"The organic compound 3-pyridylnicotinamide (3-pna), also known as N-(pyridin-3-yl)nicotinamide, is a kinked dipodal dipyridine that is synthesized through the reaction of nicotinoyl chloride and 3-aminopyridine. The nitrogen atoms on its pyridine rings, like those of its isomer 4-pyridylnicotinamide, can donate their electron lone pairs to metal cations, allowing it to bridge metal centers and act as a bidentate ligand in coordination polymers. It can be used to synthesize polymers that have potentially useful gas adsorption properties."},"fame":5,"pubchemCid":202725,"mass":199.21,"charge":0,"smiles":"C1=CC(=CN=C1)C(=O)NC2=CN=CC=C2","inchikey":"HMCAHAHCCWFPOF-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"N-pyridin-3-ylpyridine-3-carboxamide","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"202725","atoms":24,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":-0.226,"y":-1.815,"z":-0.288,"el":"O"},{"x":0.473,"y":0.394,"z":0.083,"el":"N"},{"x":3.821,"y":-1.11,"z":-0.173,"el":"N"},{"x":-4.184,"y":-0.73,"z":0.419,"el":"N"},{"x":1.885,"y":0.284,"z":0.063,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.873,"y":-0.191,"z":-0.041,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.485,"y":-0.617,"z":-0.086,"el":"C"},{"x":2.67,"y":1.402,"z":0.25,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.237,"y":1.103,"z":-0.396,"el":"C"},{"x":2.481,"y":-0.936,"z":-0.143,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.875,"y":-1.061,"z":0.356,"el":"C"},{"x":4.053,"y":1.263,"z":0.225,"el":"C"},{"x":-3.575,"y":1.482,"z":-0.344,"el":"C"},{"x":4.574,"y":-0.003,"z":0.012,"el":"C"},{"x":-4.501,"y":0.536,"z":0.066,"el":"C"},{"x":0.145,"y":1.335,"z":0.278,"el":"H"},{"x":2.231,"y":2.381,"z":0.415,"el":"H"},{"x":-1.52,"y":1.837,"z":-0.751,"el":"H